  "title": "GeoAAC and LayerRoute: Combining Geometry and Layer Routing for VLA Policies",
  "summary": "GeoAAC introduces a geometry-based adaptive action chunking method that adjusts the action horizon according to the reliability of action prediction, while LayerRoute dynamically creates action-conditioned representation routing interfaces to improve VLA policy performance. Both methods address the limitations of existing VLA frameworks by combining geometric information with flexible representation access.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "GeoAAC adjusts the action horizon to account for changing control requirements by using geometry-based information from denoising trajectories.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "LayerRoute dynamically forms mixtures of cached VLM representations and reuses intermediate action states to improve performance in VLA policies.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both methods achieve up to 7.2 gains on LIBERO Long and show improvements in real-world tasks compared to existing baselines.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
